{"units": [{"id": "zeus-note9", "translation": "where Pausanias 2, 24, 4 mentions Δία τὸν ἐν θαλάσση from Aeschylus, so that we do not know which case Aeschylus used."}, {"id": "zeus-note10", "translation": "Ζῆνα"}, {"id": "zeus-note11", "translation": "Vocative Ζεῦ"}, {"id": "zeus-note12", "translation": "In denominative and vocative Ζήν"}, {"id": "zeus-note13", "translation": "See under the word Ιώ."}, {"id": "zeus-quote1", "translation": "and one must expect that someone will be lord of Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word1", "translation": "Διός Διί Δία"}, {"id": "zeus-word2", "translation": "Ζηνός Ζηνί Ζῆνα"}, {"id": "zeus-word3", "translation": "Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word4", "translation": "of Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word5", "translation": "of Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word6", "translation": "to be lord of someone"}, {"id": "zeus-word7", "translation": "to be lord"}, {"id": "zeus-word8", "translation": "of Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word9", "translation": "of Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word10", "translation": "to Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word11", "translation": "Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word12", "translation": "Zeus in the sea"}, {"id": "zeus-word13", "translation": "Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word14", "translation": "O Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word15", "translation": "Zeus"}, {"id": "zeus-word16", "translation": "Io"}, {"id": "zephyros-orth1", "translation": "Zephyrus"}, {"id": "zephyros-def1", "translation": "Zephyrus."}, {"id": "zephyros-note1", "translation": "See under the word γίγας."}, {"id": "zephyros-quote1", "translation": "he sailed on the breeze of the giant Zephyrus"}, {"id": "zephyros-word1", "translation": "giant"}, {"id": "zeo-orth1", "translation": "to boil"}, {"id": "zeo-def1", "translation": "I boil."}, {"id": "zeo-note1", "translation": "Thus I corrected for ὀργῆς νοσούσης, about which it will be discussed under the word ὀργή."}, {"id": "zeo-quote1", "translation": "but now it still boils"}, {"id": "zeo-quote2", "translation": "words are healers of boiling anger"}, {"id": "zeo-word1", "translation": "diseased anger"}, {"id": "zeo-word2", "translation": "anger"}, {"id": "zeloo-orth1", "translation": "to deem happy"}, {"id": "zeloo-def1", "translation": "I deem happy."}, {"id": "zeloo-quote1", "translation": "I count you happy because you are free from blame"}, {"id": "zeloo-quote2", "translation": "now I count you happy in death, before seeing the depth of evils"}, {"id": "zelotos-orth1", "translation": "to be deemed happy"}, {"id": "zelotos-def1", "translation": "to be deemed happy."}, {"id": "zelotos-quote1", "translation": "being deemed happy, you led a blessed life among the Persians like a god"}, {"id": "zemia-orth1", "translation": "loss, penalty"}, {"id": "zemia-def1", "translation": "loss, penalty."}, {"id": "zemia-quote1", "translation": "a penalty is inflicted by a foolish tongue"}, {"id": "zemia-quote2", "translation": "and in eagerness and daring what penalty do you see present?"}, {"id": "zemia-quote3", "translation": "raging with penalties that bring loss of wealth"}, {"id": "zemia-quote4", "translation": "and having neglected—I will not say the penalty"}, {"id": "zeteo-orth1", "translation": "to seek"}, {"id": "zeteo-def1", "translation": "I seek."}, {"id": "zeteo-quote1", "translation": "seek some release from labors"}, {"id": "zeteo-quote2", "translation": "seek deliverance from these troubles"}, {"id": "zeteo-quote3", "translation": "and do not seek to learn your own toils"}, {"id": "zoe-orth1", "translation": "life"}, {"id": "zoe-def1", "translation": "life."}, {"id": "zoe-note1", "translation": "in Galen vol. 9 p. 385"}, {"id": "zoe-note2", "translation": "In these three places in the books Zwá and ζωῆς are written in the manuscripts, a form which the tragedians did not use, as discussed in the Thesaurus vol. 4 p. 55 after Elmsley on Eur. Med. 946."}, {"id": "zoe-quote1", "translation": "and in the earth life is mixed with murderous blood"}, {"id": "zoe-quote2", "translation": "for bitter are the vapors and not of life"}, {"id": "zoe-quote3", "translation": "death is easier than a wretched life"}, {"id": "zoe-word1", "translation": "of life"}, {"id": "zophos-orth1", "translation": "darkness"}, {"id": "zophos-def1", "translation": "darkness."}, {"id": "zophos-quote1", "translation": "under the darkness of the earth"}, {"id": "zygephoros-orth1", "translation": "yoke-bearing"}, {"id": "zygephoros-def1", "translation": "yoke-bearing, bearing a yoke."}, {"id": "zygephoros-quote1", "translation": "who had four yoke-bearing mares"}, {"id": "zygon-orth1", "translation": "yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-def1", "translation": "yoke of a chariot."}, {"id": "zygon-def2", "translation": "yoke of a balance."}, {"id": "zygon-def3", "translation": "yoke of slavery."}, {"id": "zygon-def4", "translation": "bench (of a ship)."}, {"id": "zygon-note1", "translation": "Triclinius interpolated πραθέντα τλῆναι καὶ ζυγῶν θιγεῖν βία for π. τλήναι δουλίας μάζης βία, where Engerus rightly has δουλίας μάζης τυχεῖν."}, {"id": "zygon-quote1", "translation": "and I first yoked beasts under the yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-quote2", "translation": "he breaks the middle of the yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-quote3", "translation": "yielding to this necessity, make new the yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-quote4", "translation": "and your entire yoke of the balance"}, {"id": "zygon-quote5", "translation": "may the city of Cadmus never be held under slavish yokes"}, {"id": "zygon-quote6", "translation": "to keep away the slavish yoke from this city"}, {"id": "zygon-quote7", "translation": "this city has escaped the slavish yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-quote8", "translation": "to cast a slavish yoke upon Hellas"}, {"id": "zygon-quote9", "translation": "casting a yoke upon the neck of the sea"}, {"id": "zygon-quote10", "translation": "the yoke of strength was loosed"}, {"id": "zygon-quote11", "translation": "for no one willingly uses a slavish yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-quote12", "translation": "for one must bear the slavish yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-quote13", "translation": "when those in power at the spear's yoke"}, {"id": "zygon-word1", "translation": "having been sold to endure and to touch yokes by force"}, {"id": "zygon-word2", "translation": "to endure the barley-cake of slavery by force"}, {"id": "zygon-word3", "translation": "to obtain the barley-cake of slavery"}, {"id": "zygomeo-orth1", "translation": "to yoke"}, {"id": "zygomeo-def1", "translation": "I yoke."}, {"id": "zygomeo-note1", "translation": "δαμάσω, κλείσω, καθέξω. Aeschylus in Circe satyric (fr. 113)."}, {"id": "zygomeo-quote1", "translation": "I will yoke"}, {"id": "zygomeo-word1", "translation": "I will subdue, I will shut, I will hold. Aeschylus in Circe satyric"}, {"id": "zoma-orth1", "translation": "girdle"}, {"id": "zoma-def1", "translation": "girdle (a kind of tunic)."}, {"id": "zoma-note1", "translation": "See πεζοφόρος."}, {"id": "zoma-quote1", "translation": "with girdles worn on foot"}, {"id": "zoma-word1", "translation": "wearing a girdle"}, {"id": "zone-orth1", "translation": "belt"}, {"id": "zone-def1", "translation": "belt."}, {"id": "zone-quote1", "translation": "since she carried the weight of children under her belt"}, {"id": "zone-quote2", "translation": "for how did she nourish you within, O murderer, under her belt"}, {"id": "zone-quote3", "translation": "I have cords and belts, fastenings of robes"}, {"id": "zoos-orth1", "translation": "alive"}, {"id": "zoos-def1", "translation": "alive."}, {"id": "zoos-note1", "translation": "in elegy"}, {"id": "zoos-quote1", "translation": "the fame of the dead is alive"}, {"id": "zopyreo-orth1", "translation": "to kindle"}, {"id": "zopyreo-def1", "translation": "I kindle."}, {"id": "zopyreo-quote1", "translation": "and neighboring cares kindle fear"}, {"id": "zopyreo-quote2", "translation": "of the mind being kindled"}, {"id": "zophytos-orth1", "translation": "life-giving"}, {"id": "zophytos-def1", "translation": "life-giving."}]}